post.summary:
`POST /api/maps/{id}/track-jump`, record a jump: place the system, connect it, and
link the signature it turned out to be. Member+. One command, so it undoes as one step;
it can touch a system, a connection and a signature at once, so clients just refetch.

GridConfig.description:
Map canvas geometry. Server-owned (built from env in `crate::config`), fetched by the
client so layout has a single source of truth. Node height is `2 * cell_size`;
dimensions are world-space px.

SetConnectionStatus.description:
A partial update of a connection's wormhole state. `None` leaves a field unchanged;
`Some(None)` clears it to unknown; `Some(Some(v))` sets it. Setting any field triggers
the DB sync, so linked signatures follow.
